            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.168,
            0.679,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Dhokra art is an old craft from Bihar and Odisha that uses different metals to create beautiful figures inspired by nature (Fig. 8.23). The process begins with shaping a design in beeswax. This wax model is covered with clay to make a mould. After the clay hardens, the wax is melted out, leaving a hollow space. This space is then filled with molten brass or bronze which makes Dhokra art strong and gives it a shiny golden colour. The figures often show animals, people, and nature, reflecting tribal creativity and tradition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.69,
            0.134,
            0.866,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.69,
                0.134,
                0.866,
                0.35
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.695,
                0.353,
                0.864,
                0.37
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 8.23: Dhokra art"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.41,
            0.884,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Elements and compounds are the building blocks of matter—everything that has mass and takes up space. They make the materials we see and use every day. However, not everything around us is matter. Light, heat, electricity, and even thoughts and emotions are important parts of our world, but they are not made of matter. Understanding what matter is—and what it is not—helps us better understand the world around us."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.061,
            0.542,
            0.198,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.061,
                0.542,
                0.198,
                0.677
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.56,
            0.311,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Snapshots"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.596,
            0.874,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A mixture consists two or more substances mixed together. These substances retain their individual properties and do not react chemically with each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.649,
            0.874,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The individual substances that make up a mixture are called its components."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.686,
            0.874,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A pure substance consists the same type of particles. All the constituent particles of that substance behave identically."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.722,
            0.743,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pure substance can be either an element or a compound."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.741,
            0.873,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Elements are the simplest substances that cannot be broken down further into simpler substances. They are the building blocks of all matter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.778,
            0.874,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Substances which are composed of two or more elements combined chemically in a fixed ratio and have different properties from their constituent elements are called compounds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.831,
            0.874,
            0.884
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Minerals are natural, solid substances found on the Earth. They have a fixed chemical composition. Most often they are compounds but rarely, they can also be pure elements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 16,
